            <ArticleTitle>Constrained Total Energy Expenditure and the Evolutionary Biology of Energy Balance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1249/JES.0000000000000048</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The human body adapts dynamically to maintain total energy expenditure (TEE) within a narrow physiological range. Rather than increasing with physical activity in a dose-dependent manner, experimental and ecological evidence suggests the hypothesis that TEE is a relatively constrained product of our evolved physiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
